WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.670
Not only has Netflix been spearheading a massive
change in the Hollywood marketplace as a whole,

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.260
but the digital streaming service has also
built an original programming slate that's

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.280
challenging awards season norms and giving
some beleaguered actors another shot at thriving

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.360
in the fame game.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.680
Here are some stars who've enjoyed a serious
second career wind thanks to Netflix.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.730
Adam Sandler

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.230
It's no secret that Adam Sandler's filmography
is a divisive one.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:27.550
Some of his earlier pics earned wide appreciation,
like Billy Madison, The Waterboy, and Big

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.550
Daddy.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.610
Others were passion projects built for the
critical crowd, like Punch Drunk Love and

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:32.730
Funny People.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:37.140
But some were liked by almost no one, and
since it's his commercial success that's carried

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.390
Sandler through decades of off-the-wall film
fare, that batch of box office bummers and

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.740
critical letdowns has become problematic for
Sandler.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.520
"The price is wrong, bitch."

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.870
Consider the critically obliterated Jack and
Jill and his flopped dad comedy That's My

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.870
Boy.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.600
Even his would-be smash Pixels failed to live
up to the hype, which proved, unmistakably,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.730
that Sandler's signature schtick wasn't landing
quite as well as it used to.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:06.649
But Netflix still had faith in the slapstick
comedian and provided him a platform for a

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:09.959
whopping eight movies that people are actually
watching.

00:01:09.959 --> 00:01:14.749
As of April 2017, a half billion hours of
Sandler projects had been screened on the

00:01:14.749 --> 00:01:18.520
site, between The Ridiculous 6, The Do-Over,
and Sandy Wexler.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.979
With at least a handful of Sandler films left
to go on the site, there's no doubt he's a

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:24.049
company man for Netflix now.

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:25.479
Natasha Lyonne

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:29.579
In the '90s, Natasha Lyonne was a bona fide
movie star for a brief spell, with leading

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:33.149
roles in films like Slums of Beverly Hills
and American Pie.

00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:36.770
Somewhere along the way of her gearing up
for the sequel she lost her traction in Tinseltown

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:40.759
and she started landing just bit parts in
TV shows and little-seen movies.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:44.590
But Netflix's hit series Orange is the New
Black came along at just the right time for

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.389
her, as she was still a recognizable enough
face, and her talent hadn't budged an inch

00:01:48.389 --> 00:01:50.029
in her absence from the spotlight.

00:01:50.029 --> 00:01:53.929
In the series, she stars as the troubled inmate
Nicky Nichols, who vacillates between being

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:58.170
among the most earnest and intelligent members
of the Litchfield prison population to the

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.669
most damaged and uncontrollable of the lot.

00:02:00.669 --> 00:02:04.219
It's a meaty role for Lyonne to delve into,
even if she doesn't appear in every single

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:08.090
episode, and she's started to pick up more
prestige work as a result of the series, like

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.200
a recurring role in Portlandia.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.319
Ethan Embry

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:15.799
As a child star of the '80s, Ethan Embry was
an absolute hit-maker with feel-good holiday

00:02:15.799 --> 00:02:18.450
favorites like Dutch and All I Want for Christmas.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.200
Even his teen years were kind to his career,
with his memorable supporting roles in Empire

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.579
Records, That Thing You Do!, and Can't Hardly
Wait.

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:28.730
But somewhere around the turn of the millennium,
Embry's star status started to significantly

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:29.730
fade.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:33.019
He still did enough work to keep the lights
on, of course, but the caliber of films and

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:37.030
TV shows he was earning placement in was a
far cry from the mainstream movie scene he'd

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.030
grown up in.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.359
His recurring role in Netflix's Gracie &amp; Frankie,
however, seems to be turning the tide.

00:02:42.359 --> 00:02:46.360
Not only is it the first truly regular TV
role he'd had in a decade, but it's given

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.500
him a chance to fully break away from that
wholesome, cherubic boy image he'd been associated

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.500
with for so long.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.220
"What do you mean it's looking good.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.220
That's great!

00:02:54.849 --> 00:02:55.840
We did it.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:57.069
Give me high five!"

00:02:57.069 --> 00:02:58.069
Brit Marling

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:02.311
This Chicago native has had more than her
fair share of splashy screen moments in her

00:03:02.311 --> 00:03:03.379
still-young career.

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:07.299
Count Another Earth and Sound of My Voice
among her buzziest projects.

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:11.469
But Brit Marling has still had trouble establishing
herself as a leading star, despite noteworthy

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:15.829
attempts on the indie circuit, until Netflix
came along and gave her fever dream project,

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:16.829
The OA, a chance.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:21.300
Overnight, she went from that woman you might
seen in the background of that one movie to

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.409
a completely compelling show creator and lead
star whose continued work on the series was

00:03:25.409 --> 00:03:29.430
heavily in demand for a second season, and
whose future project ideas are undoubtedly

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.639
going to get the top-of-the-pile treatment
from here on out.

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:34.030
Rosario Dawson

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:38.060
It may be hard to believe that Rosario Dawson's
career ever needed a shot in the arm.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:42.469
But after the actress hit it big with films
like Men in Black II, Seven Pounds, and Sin

00:03:42.469 --> 00:03:46.560
City, casting directors appeared to cool on
the actress for several years before she nabbed

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:51.410
a prime place in the Marvel-Netflix show universe,
starting with Daredevil in 2015.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.760
She's since reprised her role as Claire Temple
through almost all of the sister properties

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.280
and appears to be recapturing her mainstream
momentum even outside of the MCU with parts

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.639
in The LEGO Batman Movie and X-Men: The New
Mutants.

00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:03.939
Deborah Ann Woll

00:04:03.939 --> 00:04:08.920
True Blood fans were widely taken by then-newcomer
Deborah Ann Woll's vexing screen presence,

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.200
but she's had a hard time establishing herself
outside of Bon Temps ever since that HBO series

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.409
came to an end.

00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:18.079
Thanks to a series of straight-to-DVD fare,
it seemed like Woll might not ever find her

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:20.239
niche outside of the fang-banging scene.

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:25.040
Luckily, she earned a spot in Netflix's Daredevil
adaptation just in the nick of time, and now

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.380
she's spanning the Netflix-MCU series, with
her character Karen Page appearing in The

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:31.570
Punisher and The Defenders.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.639
Winona Ryder

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:37.870
For over a decade, Winona Ryder had reached
icon status in Hollywood thanks to her unforgettable

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:43.030
on-screen presence in films like Edward Scissorhands,
Beetlejuice, and Girl, Interrupted.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:48.180
But her reputation went very south in 2001
when she was caught shoplifting from a department

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.180
store.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.060
She had a great deal of trouble reaching the
A-list again after that, even despite some

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.710
notable performances in films like Black Swan
and The Iceman.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.240
But Netflix's Stranger Things has put her
right back on the map with her delightfully

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:03.520
off-kilter turn as Joyce Byers, the mother
of a boy who's been kidnapped by a toothy

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.520
monster.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.000
She's still seen as a little bit of a kook,
especially after her ultra-memeable appearance

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.070
at the SAG Awards, but thanks to Netflix she's
in the news for her acting again, instead

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.460
of her legal troubles.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.460
Thanks for watching!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.700
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.999
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

